        "payload": "tree a9063a9c75e4532f174660a7da1253ff87a4469f\nparent 2fe27be7ac98f19cbf7778f5aa7200847d17614f\nauthor George Krajcsovits <krajorama@users.noreply.github.com> 1782118826 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782118826 +0000\n\nbuild: include react-app dependency licenses in npm_licenses tarball (#18993)\n\nSince the npm-to-pnpm migration (#18797), react-app is a separate pnpm project\nwith its own web/ui/react-app/node_modules, while `npm_licenses` only scanned the\nworkspace's web/ui/node_modules. The old react-app UI is still embedded in the\nbinary (served via --enable-feature=old-ui), so its dependencies (bootstrap,\njquery, reactstrap, moment, etc.) are distributed but their licenses were dropped\nfrom npm_licenses.tar.bz2.\n\nScan react-app's node_modules too. ui-install already installs it, so the path\nexists at build time. The tarball grows from ~626 to ~1992 license files.\n\nSigned-off-by: Gy\u00f6rgy Krajcsovits <gyorgy.krajcsovits@grafana.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
